# Ctrl C stops what the shell is running and not the shell: sleep is stopped (SIGINT, so
# its status is 130), the command after it runs, and the shell takes the next line.
# files t.txt=abc
# open t.txt
# frames 9
# expect term 1 1 1
# expect termall $ echo started; sleep 30; echo status $?|started|status 130|$ echo alive|alive
1 key ` ctrl
2 text echo started; sleep 30; echo status $?
3 key enter
4 wait term started
5 wait ctrlc status 130
6 text echo alive
7 key enter
8 wait term alive
